        'id: "arbeitsagentur:12874-1643450-1-S"\ntitle: Principal Engineer Design\ncompany: Infineon Technologies AG\nurl: "https://www.arbeitsagentur.de/jobsuche/jobdetail/12874-1643450-1-S"\napply_url: "https://www.arbeitsagentur.de/jobsuche/jobdetail/12874-1643450-1-S"\nlocation: "Neubiberg, BAYERN"\ncountry: DE\nremote: false\nemployment_type: full_time\npublished_at: "2026-10-15T00:00:00+00:00"\ndescription: "#WeAreIn to draw on our creativity to develop analog and mixed-signal circuit solutions. Are you in? Your role Key responsibilities in your new role - Own end-to-end IO library design and development.- Collaborate with system architects to define and finalize IO specifications.- Lead IO integration into subsystems and provide expert guidance on IO selection, implementation, and qualification.- Drive IO quality sign-offs and ensure compliance with milestone deliverables.- Define IO architectures and align designs with product requirements.- Mentor and review team members\' work to improve design quality, performance, power, and area optimization.- Provide hands-on support for Front-End (FE) and Back-End (BE) development activities.- Enhance design and verification methodologies to improve efficiency and quality.- Ensure adherence to quality standards and development processes for library design. Your profile Qualifications and skills to help you succeed - BE/BTech/MTech in ECE, VLSI, or related field with 12+ years of IO design and development experience.- Strong expertise in IO design for LVTTL, LVCMOS, DDR, SPI, xSPI, Oscillator, LVDS, and voltage-tolerant circuits.- Good understanding of ESD (Electrostatic Discharge) and Latch-Up concepts.- Experience with IO library characterization methodologies.- Proven ability to lead small design/layout teams and drive architecture development and project planning.- Track record of delivering chip designs from specification to silicon.- Strong process management, problem-solving, multitasking, and attention to detail.- Excellent analytical, communication, and cross-functional collaboration skills. #WeAreIn for driving decarbonization and digitalization. As a global leader in semiconductor solutions in power systems and IoT, Infineon enables game-changing solutions for green and efficient energy, clean and safe mobility, as well as smart and secure IoT. Together, we drive innovation and customer success, while caring for our people and empowering them to reach ambitious goals. Be a part of making life easier, safer and greener. Are you in? We are on a journey to create the best Infineon for everyone. We strive to create the best Infineon for everyone by embracing diversity and inclusion. We welcome applicants for who they are and offer a workplace built on trust, openness, respect and equal opportunity. Our hiring decisions are based on skills and experience. Even if you don’t meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply. Please let your recruiter know if you need any accommodations during the interview process. Learn more about our various [contact channels](https://www.infineon.com/cms/en/about-infineon/company/contacts/) and about [Diversity & Inclusion](https://www.infineon.com/cms/en/careers/diversity-and-inclusion/) at Infineon."\nsalary_min: null\nsalary_max: null\nsalary_currency: null\nsalary_period: null\nprovider: arbeitsagentur\ntype: job_result\nparent_app_skill_type: app_skill_use\nembed_ref: principal-engineer-design-eYA\napp_id: jobs\nskill_id: search',
